{"game_id":2026020115,"away":"SJS","home":"NSH","split":{"name":"Pinchuk","side":1,"sec":2630},"lede":"Nashville had last change, so Andrew Brunette picked most of these matchups. Nashville played without Mavrik Bourque and William Trudeau and lost Vitali Pinchuk after 3:50 of the third. San Jose played without Darnell Nurse.","notes":[{"kind":"match","head":"The third line drew Wennberg’s line","text":"Andrew Brunette sent Marchessault, Colton and Pinchuk out for 4:18 of their 6:31 at 5-on-5 against Toffoli, Wennberg and Marchment (66%, about 27% with no line matching), and they had the worse of the chances, 0.01 to 0.42 expected goals. San Jose scored one of its three goals then."},{"kind":"match","head":"O'Reilly’s line drew Celebrini’s line","text":"Stamkos, O'Reilly and Kerfoot spent 6:45 of their 10:49 at 5-on-5 against Smith, Celebrini and Chernyshov (62%, about 27% with no line matching), and the chances were close, 0.40 to 0.34 expected goals. San Jose scored one of its three goals then."},{"kind":"exit","head":"After Pinchuk left, the lines changed","text":"Forsberg went from 29% to 50% and Kerfoot from 23% to 36% of Nashville’s 5-on-5 time, and Drury dropped from 31% to 20%."},{"kind":"result","head":"And it went better","text":"Nashville had 1.23 to 1.35 expected goals at 5-on-5 before Pinchuk left and 0.56 to 0.32 after. Nashville trailed for most of that stretch, though, and a team behind usually pushes the play, so the score explains part of it."}],"foot":"Andrew Brunette matched about as hard as in his other home games: each line spent 49% of its time against one opposing line, against 39% to 53% in his first three.","periods":{"all":{"0":{"rows":[{"label":"L1","names":["Smith","Celebrini","Chernyshov"],"sec":695,"mixed":7,"vs":[405,31,51,208],"xgf":0.51,"xga":0.79,"gf":1,"ga":0,"cells":[[0.34,0.4,1,0],[0.0,0.02,0,0],[0.13,0.0,0,0],[0.04,0.37,0,0]]},{"label":"L2","names":["Toffoli","Wennberg","Marchment"],"sec":692,"mixed":13,"vs":[112,114,258,208],"